    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for July 3rd is headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66), both of whom benefit significantly from facing favorable matchups against right-handed pitching. **Gunnar Henderson** holds our premier spot today, capitalizing on a high floor against Singer, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** finds himself in an excellent position against Mitch Keller, where park factors and a strong projected spot in the lineup bolster his efficiency. **Kyle Tucker** (71.62) remains an essential start, as his high base projection overrides any concerns regarding a tough matchup against Michael King, and **Heliot Ramos** (69.03) provides additional upside, particularly due to a favorable park environment against Feltner that elevates his overall efficiency.\n\nStrategically, the lineup construction heavily weights platoon advantages, with **Drake Baldwin** (58.44) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (59.48) anchoring the middle-tier production. Notably, the optimizer squeezed **Nasim Nunez** (56.07) into the 2B slot; while his position in the 9-hole provides a slight drag on his score, his ability to contribute to our scarcity-driven focus on stolen bases keeps him viable. Our most difficult decision on the bench was **Nolan Schanuel** (50.86), who narrowly missed the cut. Despite his solid projections, he was edged out by the superior platoon-adjusted ceiling of players like **Dominic Smith** (49.87) and **Sam Antonacci** (50.41). While **Miguel Vargas** (44.41) boasts an elite xwOBA, his current projection didn't justify displacing the higher-efficiency plays currently penciled in.\n\nInvestors should monitor the status of **Jackson Merrill** (53.24), whose lineup placement remains pending; while we assume a 6-hole assignment, any shift in his batting position against Ohtani could necessitate a late-cycle roster adjustment. Furthermore, while we are heavily invested in speed, we are cognizant of the risks; **Nasim Nunez** is flagged for facing a high-level catcher, and **Andy Pages** (64.87) must contend with King\u2019s elite ability to hold runners, which mildly suppresses his efficiency score. We will be tracking these game flows closely to maximize our 5x5 category output.",
